HowToUseIt = How to use it ?
HowToUseItDesc = You can download any list from Dolibarr in the available format(s). A button/icon is available next to each list title.
HowToUseItMore = <i>(You can change the mode from module settings)</i>
HowExportWorks = How export works ?
HowExportWorksDesc = Once you choose the export format, a small popup will show up, and all you need to do is to wait until the export process ends, after this you can download your file.
HowImportWorks = How import works?
HowImportWorksDesc = The same way, first, you choose the import format, then you should choose your import file, and wait until the import process is done, that's it.
HowImportWorksNotes = <b>Notes</b>: You should know that import process is very sensitive, so if you're not using the good import file or even your data does not fit to the table fields, then the import process may fail.<br><br><b>Cases where importation may fail</b>:<br><b>- Case</b>: You try to import an invoices list from a CSV file but you're getting errors.<br><b>* Solution</b>: You'll need to check if your CSV file data fit exactly with the table fields (you can check that on your phpmyadmin or just google it if you don't know how).<br><b>- Case</b>: You try to import your orders list on a fresh Dolibarr installation without importing products list before or even without third parties list, in this case you'll receive an error message & the importation will not work.<br><b>* Solution</b>: When you have a fresh installation of Dolibarr & you want to import your data to it, the best way to do this is to use Dolibarr database export/import tool.
INeedSomeHelp = I need some help..
INeedSomeHelpDesc = Please contact us (see about page) & we will be happy to help you.
